-a-room-2\">Present a scene to a room</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"verse-prepare: the local compression step\" href=\"/docs/guides/verse-prepare\" id=\"lnk-verse-prepare-the-local-compression-step-2\">verse-prepare: the local compression step</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"tune quality knobs\" href=\"/docs/guides/tune-quality\" id=\"lnk-tune-quality-knobs-2\">Tune quality knobs</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"run your own server\" href=\"/docs/guides/run-your-own-server\" id=\"lnk-run-your-own-server-2\">Run your own server</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"monitor production\" href=\"/docs/guides/monitor-production\" id=\"lnk-monitor-production-2\">Monitor production</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"ask verse, the site assistant\" href=\"/docs/guides/ask-verse\" id=\"lnk-ask-verse-the-site-assistant-2\">Ask Verse, the site assistant</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"verse home: floor plan to 3d home\" href=\"/docs/guides/floor-plan-to-3d\" id=\"lnk-verse-home-floor-plan-to-3d-home-2\">Verse Home: floor plan to 3D home</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"verse home: plan to a home buyers walk, restyle and tour\" href=\"/docs/guides/instant-home\" id=\"lnk-verse-home-plan-to-a-home-buyers-walk-re-2\">Verse Home: plan to a home buyers walk, restyle and tour</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"&lt;verse-viewer&gt;: one tag, any page\" href=\"/docs/guides/web-component\" id=\"lnk-one-tag-any-page-2\">&lt;verse-viewer&gt;: one tag, any page</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"designer tools: framer, webflow, figma\" href=\"/docs/guides/designer-tools\" id=\"lnk-designer-tools-framer-webflow-figma-2\">Designer tools: Framer, Webflow, Figma</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"react and vue wrappers\" href=\"/docs/guides/react-and-vue\" id=\"lnk-react-and-vue-wrappers-2\">React and Vue wrappers</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"rest client round trip\" href=\"/docs/guides/rest-client\" id=\"lnk-rest-client-round-trip-2\">REST client round trip</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"sell with woocommerce\" href=\"/docs/guides/sell-with-woocommerce\" id=\"lnk-sell-with-woocommerce-2\">Sell with WooCommerce</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"sell with bigcommerce\" href=\"/docs/guides/sell-with-bigcommerce\" id=\"lnk-sell-with-bigcommerce-2\">Sell with BigCommerce</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"sell with magento / adobe commerce\" href=\"/docs/guides/sell-with-magento\" id=\"lnk-sell-with-magento-adobe-commerce-2\">Sell with Magento / Adobe Commerce</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"embed in wix\" href=\"/docs/guides/embed-in-wix\" id=\"lnk-embed-in-wix-2\">Embed in Wix</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"embed in squarespace\" href=\"/docs/guides/embed-in-squarespace\" id=\"lnk-embed-in-squarespace-2\">Embed in Squarespace</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"embed in framer\" href=\"/docs/guides/embed-in-framer\" id=\"lnk-embed-in-framer-2\">Embed in Framer</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"embed in ghost and hubspot\" href=\"/docs/guides/embed-in-ghost-and-hubspot\" id=\"lnk-embed-in-ghost-and-hubspot-2\">Embed in Ghost and HubSpot</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"automate with zapier\" href=\"/docs/guides/automate-with-zapier\" id=\"lnk-automate-with-zapier-2\">Automate with Zapier</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"automate with make\" href=\"/docs/guides/automate-with-make\" id=\"lnk-automate-with-make-2\">Automate with Make</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"automate with n8n\" href=\"/docs/guides/automate-with-n8n\" id=\"lnk-automate-with-n8n-2\">Automate with n8n</a></section><section id=\"sec-item-10\"><h2>Blog & updates</h2><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"all posts\" href=\"/docs/blog/index\" id=\"lnk-all-posts-2\">All posts</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"how verse streams a building\" href=\"/docs/blog/how-verse-streams-a-building\" id=\"lnk-how-verse-streams-a-building-2\">How Verse streams a building</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"2.7: what's new for you\" href=\"/docs/blog/verse-engine-2-7-whats-new\" id=\"lnk-2-7-what-s-new-for-you-2\">2.7: what's new for you</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"2.0 release notes for humans\" href=\"/docs/blog/2-0-release-notes-for-humans\" id=\"lnk-2-0-release-notes-for-humans-2\">2.0 release notes for humans</a></section><section id=\"sec-item-11\"><h2>Integrations</h2><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"integrations: every platform at a glance\" href=\"/docs/integrations\" id=\"lnk-integrations-every-platform-at-a-glance-2\">Integrations: every platform at a glance</a></section><section id=\"sec-item-12\"><h2>API & SDK</h2><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"verse api, sdk and mcp: embed, sdk, webhooks\" href=\"/docs/developers\" id=\"lnk-verse-api-sdk-and-mcp-embed-sdk-webhooks-2\">Verse API, SDK and MCP: embed, SDK, webhooks</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"verse api reference\" href=\"/docs/api\" id=\"lnk-verse-api-reference-2\">Verse API reference</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"api quickstart\" href=\"/docs/api-quickstart\" id=\"lnk-api-quickstart-2\">API quickstart</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"api changelog\" href=\"/docs/api-changelog\" id=\"lnk-api-changelog-2\">API changelog</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"embed sdk reference\" href=\"/docs/embed-sdk\" id=\"lnk-embed-sdk-reference-2\">Embed SDK reference</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"verse sdk: js / ts (@ctruhtech/verse-sdk)\" href=\"/docs/sdk\" id=\"lnk-verse-sdk-js-ts-ctruhtech-verse-sdk-2\">Verse SDK: JS / TS (@ctruhtech/verse-sdk)</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"verse mcp server for ai agents\" href=\"/docs/mcp\" id=\"lnk-verse-mcp-server-for-ai-agents-2\">Verse MCP server for AI agents</a></section><p class=\"docs-no-results\" hidden>No matching guides.</p></div></nav></aside><div class=\"doc-body\"><article class=\"doc-article\" id=\"art-doc-article\"><h1 id=\"see-it-in-your-room-view-in-ar-on-a-phone\">See it in your room — View in AR on a phone<a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#see-it-in-your-room-view-in-ar-on-a-phone\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\" id=\"lnk-link-to-this-section\">#</a></h1>\n<p><em>A product-scale scene (a chair, a lamp, a watch, a chess set) can be placed\non a real table from its share link. Nothing to install: the scene&#39;s own\npage shows <strong>View in AR</strong> on phones that can do it.</em></p>\n<h2 id=\"what-the-visitor-gets\">What the visitor gets<a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#what-the-visitor-gets\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\" id=\"lnk-link-to-this-section-2\">#</a></h2>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr><th>Phone</th><th>What happens on <strong>View in AR</strong></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Android, Chrome</strong> (and other WebXR-capable browsers)</td><td>The page opens a WebXR AR session. A white ring follows the surfaces the camera finds; <strong>tap</strong> places the object on it, <strong>one finger</strong> turns it, <strong>pinch</strong> resizes it (the readout shows the factor), <strong>Reset</strong> picks it up again, <strong>Exit AR</strong> returns to the page. The object is the same streamed scene the page was showing — it keeps streaming detail while you look at it, and the room&#39;s light level nudges its exposure.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>iPhone / iPad, Safari</strong></td><td>The control is Apple&#39;s AR Quick Look link: Safari opens the scene&#39;s <code>.usdz</code> in AR with its own placement, scale and share sheet.</td></tr><tr><td>Desktop, or a phone without AR</td><td>No control is shown.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p>The control appears only for <strong>product-scale</strong> scenes: the compile-time\nstaging says <code>kind: &quot;object&quot;</code>, or — for open / pre-<code>kind</code> scenes — the\nscene is at most 6 m across. Interiors are walked through (and viewed in a\nheadset), never placed on a table.</p>\n<h2 id=\"what-the-server-builds\">What the server builds<a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#what-the-server-builds\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\" id=\"lnk-link-to-this-section-3\">#</a></h2>\n<p>When a scene compiles, the ingest route also writes <strong><code>ingest/&lt;id&gt;.usdz</code></strong>\n— the iOS AR Quick Look package — from the prepared GLB, right before the\nsource file is deleted. It is served exactly like the scene&#39;s other\nartifacts (<code>model/vnd.usdz+zip</code>, immutable, same visibility: a private\nscene&#39;s package needs the owner&#39;s cookie or the share token; it follows the\nscene&#39;s version with <code>?v=</code>), and the finished job record says so:</p>\n<div class=\"doc-code\" data-lang=\"json\"><div><span>Code</span><button type=\"button\" data-copy-local id=\"btn-copy\">Copy ⧉</button></div><pre><code class=\"lang-json\">{ &quot;status&quot;: &quot;done&quot;, &quot;vpkUrl&quot;: &quot;…/ingest/chair-1a2b3c4d5e6f.vpk&quot;,\n  &quot;arUrl&quot;:  &quot;https://HOST/ingest/chair-1a2b3c4d5e6f.usdz&quot;,\n  &quot;ar&quot;:     { &quot;bytes&quot;: 13122418, &quot;triangles&quot;: 76920, &quot;textures&quot;: 9, &quot;resized&quot;: 0, &quot;seconds&quot;: 0.05 } }</code></pre></div>\n<p>or, when there is none, why: <code>&quot;ar&quot;: { &quot;skipped&quot;: &quot;an interior is walked\nthrough, not placed in a room&quot; }</code>, <code>&quot;… over the 150 MB AR cap&quot;</code>, <code>&quot;…\nover the 5 M AR cap&quot;</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>Caps</strong> (<code>web/playground/usdz.mjs</code>, <code>USDZ_LIMITS</code>): a prepared GLB of at\nmost <strong>150 MB</strong> and <strong>5 M triangles</strong>; PNG textures wider than <strong>2048 px</strong>\nare downsampled in the package (JPEGs stay as encoded — <code>verse-prepare</code>\nalready caps them at 4096 on ingest). The three bundled demos convert in\nunder 0.1 s each (chess set 76.9 k tris → 12.5 MB; marble bust 17.5 k tris\n→ 6.5 MB; antique camera 20 k tris → 18.7 MB); the package is text USDA\nplus the images, so it is larger than the <code>.vpk</code>. <code>VERSE_AR=0</code> turns the\npackaging off on a server.</p>\n<p>The converter is pure Node — no native dependency, nothing to install on\nthe server — and the packages pass Apple&#39;s own validator\n(<code>usdchecker --arkit</code>, which macOS ships). What it carries: every mesh\ninstance with its world transform, vertex normals and <code>st</code> texcoords,\n<code>UsdPreviewSurface</code> materials with base colour, metallic-roughness, normal,\nocclusion and emissive textures, alpha blend / mask, double-sided. What it\nleaves out (honest list): animations and skins (bind pose only),\n<code>KHR_texture_transform</code>, vertex colours, sparse accessors, KTX2 textures\n(factors only — the compact atlas tier is not an image Quick Look reads).</p>\n<h2 id=\"for-developers\">For developers<a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#for-developers\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\" id=\"lnk-link-to-this-section-4\">#</a></h2>\n<ul><li><strong>API:</strong> <code>arUrl</code> / <code>ar</code> on the finished job record\n(<a href=\"/docs/api#get-v1-ingest-job\" id=\"lnk-api-md-get-v1-ingest\">api.md § GET /v1/ingest/&lt;job&gt;</a>); the file\nitself at <code>GET /ingest/&lt;id&gt;.usdz</code>.</li><li><strong>SDK:</strong> <code>verse.scenes.arUrl(id, { share?, version? })</code> builds the link —\nput it in <code>&lt;a rel=&quot;ar&quot; href=&quot;…&quot;&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;poster.png&quot;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;</code> on your own\npage and Safari opens it in AR (<a href=\"/docs/sdk#scenes-arurl-id-share-version-get-ingest-id-usdz\" id=\"lnk-sdk-md\">sdk.md</a>).</li><li><strong>Embed:</strong> the viewer shows its own <strong>View in AR</strong> control inside the\nframe; the <code>stage</code> event&#39;s <code>ar</code> field tells your page which path the\ndevice has (<code>&quot;webxr&quot;</code>, <code>&quot;quicklook&quot;</code> or <code>null</code>), <code>viewer.enterAR()</code>\nstarts it and <code>ar</code> events report what happened\n(<a href=\"/docs/embed-sdk#enterar\" id=\"lnk-embed-sdk-md\">embed-sdk.md</a>). WebXR needs a tap <em>inside</em> the\nframe: a programmatic <code>enterAR()</code> on Android may report <code>state:\n&quot;blocked&quot;</code>; the in-frame button always works.</li><li><strong>Links:</strong> nothing to add — the share link shows the control on its own.</li></ul>\n<h2 id=\"how-the-webxr-path-renders-and-its-honest-limits\">How the WebXR path renders (and its honest limits)<a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#how-the-webxr-path-renders-and-its-honest-limits\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\" id=\"lnk-link-to-this-section-5\">#</a></h2>\n<p>The session reuses the headset plumbing (<code>web/playground/xr.js</code>): the\nengine&#39;s mono loop is suspended, every XR frame&#39;s camera pose crosses to\nthe render worker as an <code>xr-frame</code> (the same pose for both &quot;eyes&quot; — the\nstereo path is the engine&#39;s one external-camera path), and a WebGL2\npresenter on the main thread samples the left half of the engine canvas\ninto the <code>XRWebGLLayer</code>. The camera feed shows through where the engine\npainted its backdrop: the session sets the solid backdrop (<code>?bg=</code>&#39;s lane)\nto a chroma key (<code>#00ff00</code>, pure green) and the presenter keys it to alpha 0. That is\nthe v1 of a transparent clear — exact on the flat backdrop, with a\nnarrow halo possible on anti-aliased silhouettes against it; a true alpha\nrender target is the follow-up (backlog). Placement is a model matrix\nfolded into the view matrix (the object&#39;s base centre on the hit pose, the\nturn and the pinch scale), so the engine streams and culls exactly as it\ndoes on the page. Light estimation (<code>XRLightProbe</code>&#39;s primary intensity)\nnudges the engine&#39;s exposure by at most ±1.5 EV, smoothed.</p>\n<p>Offered on browsers with WebGPU only — the stereo path renders the session;\nthe WebGL2 build shows no WebXR control (iOS Safari uses Quick Look on\nevery device). Temporal mode (<code>?temporal=</code>) is refused like VR.</p>\n<h2 id=\"what-is-proven-and-what-needs-a-phone\">What is proven, and what needs a phone<a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#what-is-proven-and-what-needs-a-phone\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\" id=\"lnk-link-to-this-section-6\">#</a></h2>\n<p><code>web/test/fix-verify-ar.mjs</code> (ports 8820–8829) proves, headlessly: the\npackage is built through the real ingest route, is a valid USDZ (stored\nentries, 64-byte alignment, CRCs, the USDA first), references every\nmaterial and texture, is under the cap, passes <code>usdchecker --arkit</code>; an\ninterior gets none; the control is an <code>&lt;a rel=&quot;ar&quot;&gt;</code> with its <code>&lt;img&gt;</code> on an\nemulated iPhone and absent on desktop; with <code>navigator.xr</code> stubbed, the\nWebXR button appears, <code>requestSession</code> asks for <code>immersive-ar</code> with\n<code>hit-test</code> required and <code>dom-overlay</code> + <code>light-estimation</code> optional, the\nrenderer switches to the AR clear mode (suspend → AR-size resize → chroma\nkey backdrop), stubbed frames produce <code>xr-frame</code> poses, a tap places, a\npinch scales, exit restores everything; the embed&#39;s <code>stage.ar</code> and\n<code>enterAR()</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>Only a phone can prove</strong> that ARCore finds the plane and the keyed frame\ncomposites cleanly over the camera feed, that Safari hands the link to AR\nQuick Look and places the object at true scale, and what real-room light\nestimates look like. Test plan for the first device pass: open\n<code>/view?vpk=ingest/demo-chess-set.vpk</code> on an Android phone in Chrome → View\nin AR → place on a table (the board should be 55 cm across); on an iPhone\n→ View in AR → Quick Look opens; both paths on a private scene with\n<code>?share=</code>.</p></article><div class=\"doc-source\">Published documentation from <a href=\"https://verse.ctruh.com/docs/#/guides/view-in-ar\" id=\"lnk-verse-by-ctruh\">Verse by Ctruh</a></div></div><aside class=\"docs-toc\" id=\"asd-docs-toc\"><p>ON THIS PAGE</p><a href=\"#what-the-visitor-gets\" id=\"lnk-what-the-visitor-gets\">What the visitor gets</a><a href=\"#what-the-server-builds\" id=\"lnk-what-the-server-builds\">What the server builds</a><a href=\"#for-developers\" id=\"lnk-for-developers\">For developers</a><a href=\"#how-the-webxr-path-renders-and-its-honest-limits\" id=\"lnk-how-the-webxr-path-renders-and-its-hones\">How the WebXR path renders (and its honest limits)</a><a href=\"#what-is-proven-and-what-needs-a-phone\" id=\"lnk-what-is-proven-and-what-needs-a-phone\">What is proven, and what needs a phone</a></aside></section>"}